  designNotes: "Beat 6: stage boss. Default squad is 6 rifle + 2 rocket — the keep
    is the first masonry the player is handed the tool for. The first BossPhaseTrigger the project has ever
    fired \u2014 the keep falling spawns the Citadel Sovereign (260 hp) and a heavy
    escort, so the level does not end when the structure does. Biome reuses Mountains
    from beat 1 on purpose: same ground, a fortress instead of a hut, which is the
    clearest possible read on how far the player has come. Structure hp RETUNED 2026-08-07:
    bunker and keep both hpScale 0.66 (180 -> 118, 212 -> 139), garrisoned total
    392 -> 257. Scaled TOGETHER so the keep stays the dominant structure; 257 leaves
    a stage boss less slack than the levels before it, which is the point. BOSS SPAWN MOVED 2026-08-12: the heavy escort was at anchorX 3 and TWO of its
    three men stood inside MountainBunker's box (x[0.88,3.13]) - the bunker is NOT this phase's
    trigger, so it is still standing when they arrive and they could not be hit. Escort moved to
    4.5 and the Sovereign from 5 to 6.5 so the two groups do not stand on each other. Both now
    land in the KEEP's footprint, which is rubble by definition at that moment - the keep is
    what triggers the phase - so they emerge from the breach, which is what the beat wanted
    anyway. Found because rule 8 was extended to mid-battle arrivals; it had only ever measured
    turn 0."
